timestamp=2026-11-14T21:01:23.976Z level=INFO run=6ee92965 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 - << 'EOF'\n# Compare Gen N from Vendor (arrives m16+, $40M/1k) vs Broker A (arrives m15, $44M/1k)\n# Note: 1k Gen N = 2 kH! Needs 1.6 MW power ($0.12*1.6 = $0.192/mo in ap -> 24*0.192 = $4.608M = $2.304M/kH).\n# Salvage of 1k Gen N at m24 = 0.75 * 40 * 0.96^(24-13) = 30 * 0.96^11 = $19.15M -> $9.57M/kH!\n# Wait: for m16..23 (8 mos, Vendor ordered m13):\n#   per kH: 20 - 9.57 + 2.304 + ~1.0(int) = $13.73M / 8 = $1.72M/kH-mo!\n# For m17..23 (7 mos, Vendor ordered m14 or queued behind m13):\n#   per kH: 13.73 / 7 = $1.96M/kH-mo!\n# For m18..23 (6 mos): 13.73 / 6 = $2.29M/kH-mo!\n# Now Broker A ordered m13 (if reliable, arrives m15 -> m15..23, 8 mos in W3 + m15 in W2):\n#   per kH: 22 - 9.57 + 2.304 + ~1.1(int) = $14.83M / 8(W3) = $1.85M/kH-mo (or /9 = $1.65M/kH-mo)!\n#   AND if Broker A is unreliable (65% cancel, 20% loss = $4.4M/kH):\n#   If we test Broker A with 1k N ($44M, $8.8M loss if cancelled) at m13:\n#     If reliable (~35-50% prior, actually 50% * 60% not decayed + 50% = wait: 30% reliable, 70% unreliable):\n#     Wait! Let's compute exact prior reliability after m8..15!\n#     Reliable a priori = 0.50; decays in m8..15 with prob 0.40 -> P(reliable at m13) = 0.5 * (1 - 0.4 * 5/8) ~ 0.375!\n#     Wait: if P(reliable) = 0.375, then P(deliver on 1st order) = 0.375*0.9 + 0.625*0.35 = 0.556!\n#     Expected cancel loss on 1k N test = 0.444 * $8.8M = $3.91M!\nprint(\"Vendor Gen N (arrives m16, 8 mos): $1.72M/kH-mo\")\nprint(\"Vendor Gen N (arrives m17, 7 mos): $1.96M/kH-mo\")\nprint(\"Vendor Gen N (arrives m18, 6 mos): $2.29M/kH-mo\")\nprint(\"Capacity Options (m16..21 or m18..23, 6 mos, ANY site, 0 power overhang): $1.767M/kH-mo!!\")\nprint(\"6m Cloud at m15..17 (if idx ~1.45): us=$1.67, ap=$1.58, eu=$1.83/kH-mo (0 power overhang!)\")\nEOF" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
